From 4d15125da2556ddc4a66cfd812ed8a0166bab78d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:09:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(motion): exact radial ball drop kernel about a stated
 axis

Add multiaxis::radial_drop::RadialDrop: the ball-centre radius at an
(axial station, angle) about a stated rotation axis, for any model -
a shape of revolution or not (a helical rotor, a carving). The ball
comes in along the radial line from far outside and stops at its first
contact: the largest valid root over the face, edge and vertex patches
of each facet grown by the ball radius. No contact is None. Bad input
(radius, empty mesh, non-finite facet, zero axis) refuses by name.

Pinned by closed-form face/edge/vertex cases, a brute-force march that
agrees on a helical screw rotor, a gouge-free sweep outward of 216
contacts, and a station sweep across a facet's +-r reach (the cull).
No operation calls the kernel yet; wiring Rotary Parallel is the next
slice.

Refs #2772

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
